>It seems like it doesn't
>matter how low my AC is or how +'ed my weapon is, I get worn down. 

Two questions: 
1) How low do you consider a "low" AC to be? Something less than -30
is pretty much mandatory. If I have close to -40 AC, I rarely lose
more than 30 points or so (out of 200+) in any scuffle. 
2) How much are you fighting? Your goal, once you get the Amulet, is
not to fight with every monster you see; it's to get out of there in
one piece! It sounds like you're just fighting too much.

A couple of suggestions for avoiding fights in two critical times:
have a means of teleport control and level-teleport to use just after
you get the Book from Rodney. Levelport down to the vibrating square
level. Then teleport directly to the vibrating square. Two turns after
getting the Book, you're ready to do the invocation.

Also, have a cursed potion of gain level ready for when you've
snatched the Amulet. You'll rise through the ceiling and avoid having
to fight your way out of the Sanctum.

>This time I tried to bring more escape mechanisms--/oTele, ?oTele,
>/oDig.  But I could never have too many handy else I was burdened.  Or
>they were destroyed by fire traps.  

Your wands won't get destroyed by fire traps. Keep one outside your
BoH, the rest inside. Make sure they're ID'd so you know how many
charges you have; don't leave yourself in a crisis with an empty wand.

>I was told once about level teleporting.   It would be nice to just
>grab the AoY and tele the hell out of Geh.  But how do you do this?  I
>thought you couldn't level tele with the AoY anyway.

You can't levelport once you have the Amulet; however, you can
teleport directly to the stairs of whatever level you're on--again, if
you have teleport control. Seems to fail sometimes, once you have the
Amulet, but it works often enough to be useful.

Even on non-teleport levels, you can use wands to teleport monsters
away from yourself.

Keep out of fights, and you should be okay.

